Z||000000||ChadMan||04-10-2000||11:19 AM||||Back in the summer of 98 I was looking for a rt-side door skin for my 86 SE.  It had to be red because the rest of the car had good paint and I didn't want to paint it.  I wound up paying $125 for a whole door from a junkyard - they wouldn't sell just the skin.  I was proud of myself for saving the cost of a paint job.<P>Now I see this on eBay - currently $5!  D'oh!!!  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=305147048" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=305147048</A> <P>Anybody else ever pay way more than a Fiero part is worth?||||reg||9
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-10-2000||11:44 AM||||I'm sorry to say, but that auction just started and it could easily go to !50.00. Some of the wrecking yards in the bay area sell those door skins from any where $50.00 to $100.00. It is worth what you arewilling to pay for. How badly do I want this item? How badly do I need this item. Remember that half the time you buy and item and you still have to modify it.ie: paint You got lucky at the price you paid and you did not have to repaint. I sell door skins for fifty and 90% of the time you have to get it painted and the cost to paint a door skin to match is $150.00 So count your blessings||||reg||1
